    {
       "name": "Emergency calls",
       "description": "An emergency call center (the French 15/112). Level 1 operators screen the calls: advice they give themselves, urgent calls they transfer to level 2 and hang up, critical calls they keep until a level 2 operator joins (three-way call). Press Space and fire the transitions: who waits, and where? The colors are the kinds of calls for the runtime (EmergencyCalls.cpp).",
       "colors": ["Advice", "Urgent", "Critical"],
       "places": [
            { "id": 0, "caption": "Call screening", "tokens": 0 },
            { "id": 1, "caption": "Waiting for a three-way call", "tokens": 0 },
